<h2 id="includes">What an MSO Handles</h2>
<p>Adding regenerative medicine to a practice creates a second business inside your business — with its own protocol, its own documentation requirements, its own staffing and reporting. An MSO relationship takes on that operational layer so it runs the same way every day, whether or not you're the one watching it.</p>

<h3>Operational Scope</h3>
<div class="dash-list">
  <div class="dash-list-item">Administrative and back-office operations for the regenerative service line</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">AAAHC-aligned policies, procedures, and ongoing compliance management</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Staffing support and competency tracking across the team</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Outcome tracking, KPI reporting, and quality management</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Standardization of the one consistent protocol across every case</div>
</div>

<h2 id="control">What Stays With You</h2>
<p>You retain full clinical authority and ownership of your practice. Regenitiva does not practice medicine and does not make clinical decisions. The MSO manages the operational structure around the program — the machinery — while every treatment decision remains yours.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Why this matters</div>
  <p class="callout-body">Most programs stall not because the medicine is hard, but because the operations are. An MSO relationship means the compliance, documentation, and reporting are handled by a team that does this full-time, instead of being absorbed by staff who already have a full day.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="how">How the Relationship Works</h2>
<p>An MSO engagement is scoped to what your practice actually needs. Some groups hand over the full operational layer; others keep more in-house and use Regenitiva for specific functions.</p>

<div class="numbered-steps">
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">1</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Assessment</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">We review your current staffing, space, insurance coverage, and local demographics to understand what the program needs to run well.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">2</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Scope &amp; Structure</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">We define which operational functions Regenitiva manages and which stay in-house, and put the supporting documentation in place.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">3</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Ongoing Management</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">Compliance, reporting, and operational standards are maintained continuously, with the team trained and supported as the program grows.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 id="related">Related Services</h2>
<p>An MSO relationship often draws on <a href="/services/operations-compliance">Practice Operations &amp; Compliance</a>, <a href="/services/outcome-tracking">Outcome Tracking &amp; Data Analytics</a>, and <a href="/services/multi-clinic-management">Multi-Clinic Management</a>. If you're running more than one location, those pages are worth a look.</p>

<h2 id="start">Getting Started</h2>
<p>The first step is an introductory conversation — a short call with our CEO, Vince Surra, to talk through whether a practice assessment makes sense for you. There's no commitment attached to it.</p>
<p>Reach out through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> and we'll be in touch within one business day, usually sooner, or book a call directly.</p>

